From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lazar Gopcevic <lazgop@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 12:29:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(claude-native): follow CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR instead of
 ~/.claude

Not upstream yet: tracked by issue https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/issues/7124;
upstream PR #9617, which carried it, was closed without merging. The
account work below needs it.

Claude Code takes its profile from CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR. The runner env
forwards it and trust seeding follows it, but the rest of what Omnigent
reads and writes on Claude's behalf was still pinned to ~/.claude: the
user settings behind the status line and effort level, the transcript
lookup used when a session moves, the claude-sdk sandbox's writable
roots and files, and the install ledger's check for the omnigent MCP
entry. Under a selected profile each of these looked at the wrong one.

Resolve all of them through claude_paths, so a single rule decides
where Claude's files live. Keep tests that pin the
CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR passthrough through both env strips, since the
claude-native pane depends on it too.

Tests now clear CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR by default, so a developer's own
profile cannot slip past the tmp-HOME isolation the suite relies on.

Replayed onto current main from #7125 (Lazar Gopcevic): the Claude-native
test modules moved to tests/harnesses/claude_native/ and
tests/inner/test_claude_sdk_executor.py gained tests at the same insertion
point. ensure_claude_workspace_trusted keeps main's inline resolution, which
already follows CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and which #9583 is reworking.

An e2e_ui journey opens a claude-native session in the SPA with
CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR exported, attaches the Terminal view to the real Claude TUI
and asserts the status bar chains the selected profile's statusLine while the
default ~/.claude profile carries a decoy. The unit tests for the settings
reader and transcript lookup use the same two-profile setup.

Signed-off-by: Lazar Gopcevic <lazgop@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 3b60158eab69a9d4f08a4e3b45a030985394de19)
Signed-off-by: omni-resolve-agent[bot] <omni-resolve-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Docs: none (fix: Omnigent follows Claude Code's own CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, as the CLI does; no new setting)
